 "result": "I fixed the rounding bug in `calc/pricing.py`, and `test_discount_rounding` now passes.\n\n**Cause:** `apply_discount` cut off the extra decimals with `int(... * 100) / 100` instead of rounding. Floating-point maths makes `2.30 * 0.5 * 100` come out as `114.99999\u2026`, so cutting it off gave `1.14` instead of `1.15`.\n\n**Fix:** I changed line 7 to round to two decimal places:\n```python\nreturn round(price * (1 - pct / 100), 2)\n```\n\nResult: `python3 -m unittest -v tests.test_pricing.TestPricing.test_discount_rounding` ran 1 test, OK. I didn't run the other test, `test_no_discount`, after the change; it passed before it.",
